{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/379105-is-werewolf-going-to-have-a-more-defined-version-of-influence","id":379105,"title":"Is Werewolf going to have a more defined version of Influence?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-23T09:54:00-08:00","id":379105,"title":"Is Werewolf going to have a more defined version of Influence?","content":"Alright, from a variety of spoilers it's pretty clear that Uratha are going to have access to a variety of different Influences.<br /> <br /> Will the Werewolf 2e books go into more detail in what you can do with them? I mean, they were initially designed for NPCs, and are therefor pretty rules-light; given how rules-heavy everything else is, it stands out when players get it.<br /> <br /> Will we get examples of what's appropriate with each level? Like how big a bonus you can give with Strengthen, and stuff like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T11:30:17-08:00","id":379238,"title":"","content":"Do you mean spirit influence or social influence?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T11:37:31-08:00","id":379247,"title":"","content":"Probably spirit influence, what with the references to Strengthen.<br /> <br /> I think it's based on your Power+Finesse roll, though I don't know what the werewolf equivalent is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T12:10:33-08:00","id":379318,"title":"","content":"We've been specifically told that W2e's equivalent of the Ephemeral Beings rules focuses entirely on spirits, which I imagine should help somewhat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T14:00:15-08:00","id":379498,"title":"","content":"Here's to hoping! I really just want examples so I know what kind of bonuses I should award with Strengthen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-24T08:34:25-08:00","id":380132,"title":"","content":"I usually rule it as it awarding +1 per dot in the influence. I think the influence chart in one of the versions said that it grants a bonus equal to rank. Lore of the Forsaken also has a section on artificial spirits near the end, and it describes how much essence to spend to get what particular favors out of spirits of various ranks - which makes a fairly handy supplement to the Influences chart. I've also looked at Mage practices for some parallels as to what influences can do, especially for Manipulation [although I know this is technically incorrect, as Imperial Mysteries says it takes 6 dots in Influence to have the free form of a Mage arcana. but I don't see a <i>good </i>reason for that in many cases.]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T02:36:29-08:00","id":380870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/379105-is-werewolf-going-to-have-a-more-defined-version-of-influence?p=380132#post380132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've also looked at Mage practices for some parallels as to what influences can do, especially for Manipulation [although I know this is technically incorrect, as Imperial Mysteries says it takes 6 dots in Influence to have the free form of a Mage arcana. but I don't see a <i>good </i>reason for that in many cases.]</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because Influences are seldom as broad as Arcana. If you have Influences in Shadows, how many dots in it do you need to be able to do something like the things Death can do with them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T08:11:35-08:00","id":381018,"title":"","content":"A thing about Influences is that, because they're so wide-ranging in possibilities (you can have an Influence of just about anything) it's hard to come up with a really rigid structure for exactly what each Influence can do. I personally prefer to play a bit more fast and loose with them, hence I had a Hunger-Claimed Strengthen the 'hunger' of a car's engine recently to make it guzzle through fuel at a ridiculous rate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T08:47:10-08:00","id":381036,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'd assume a spirit of 'reflections' in the literal sense (IE, how light it perceived) with Control, could make people invisible by virtue of displacing their reflections from eye irises into other reflective surfaces.<br /> <br /> Here's my gripe with the current description of Influences, tho: When can a spirit of say, Hunger, diminish it? Would that be within the grounds of Manipulation? If so, in order to do say, use 'Destruction' as influence, given that Create is rank 4, then Destruction would be rank 5. Mass Destruction would be, therefore... Rank 6. Works?<br /> <br /> Or are spirits fundamentally conceaved under the impression that natural bans would prevent a spirit of say, hunger to even conceive the notion of lowering said hunger? I think that makes them way too one dimentional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T13:58:44-08:00","id":381328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/379105-is-werewolf-going-to-have-a-more-defined-version-of-influence?p=381018#post381018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A thing about Influences is that, because they're so wide-ranging in possibilities (you can have an Influence of just about anything) it's hard to come up with a really rigid structure for exactly what each Influence can do. I personally prefer to play a bit more fast and loose with them, hence I had a Hunger-Claimed Strengthen the 'hunger' of a car's engine recently to make it guzzle through fuel at a ridiculous rate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really just want examples, not a rigid structure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T17:36:20-08:00","id":382505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/379105-is-werewolf-going-to-have-a-more-defined-version-of-influence?p=380132#post380132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've also looked at Mage practices for some parallels as to what influences can do, especially for Manipulation [although I know this is technically incorrect, as Imperial Mysteries says it takes 6 dots in Influence to have the free form of a Mage arcana. but I don't see a <i>good </i>reason for that in many cases.]</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't read the book, but do you mean that they gain Compelling, Knowing, Unveiling, Ruling, Veiling, and so on equivalents for their Influence, or they get like Spirit \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T04:35:56-08:00","id":382927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/379105-is-werewolf-going-to-have-a-more-defined-version-of-influence?p=381036#post381036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I'd assume a spirit of 'reflections' in the literal sense (IE, how light it perceived) with Control, could make people invisible by virtue of displacing their reflections from eye irises into other reflective surfaces.<br /> <br /> Here's my gripe with the current description of Influences, tho: When can a spirit of say, Hunger, diminish it? Would that be within the grounds of Manipulation? If so, in order to do say, use 'Destruction' as influence, given that Create is rank 4, then Destruction would be rank 5. Mass Destruction would be, therefore... Rank 6. Works?<br /> <br /> Or are spirits fundamentally conceaved under the impression that natural bans would prevent a spirit of say, hunger to even conceive the notion of lowering said hunger? I think that makes them way too one dimentional.</div> </div> </div> </div>Off the top of my head, not looking at the actual Influence rules, I'd suggest Manipulate or Control could diminish to some extent, so 2 or 3 dots. I'd certainly expect the old 3-dot Control Fire Elemental Gift to let you quench flame, and that was basically 'Influence: Fire 3'.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/379105-is-werewolf-going-to-have-a-more-defined-version-of-influence?p=381328#post381328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really just want examples, not a rigid structure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok. You'll have to wait and see what Mr. Brookshaw put into the spirit rules section. If it's not to your satisfaction, then when the book comes out we should totally do a thread with ideas for lots of different Influences and what they can do at each dot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T04:52:35-08:00","id":382939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/379105-is-werewolf-going-to-have-a-more-defined-version-of-influence?p=382505#post382505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I haven't read the book, but do you mean that they gain Compelling, Knowing, Unveiling, Ruling, Veiling, and so on equivalents for their Influence, or they get like Spirit \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, they get the full shebang; I've never personally liked that, since there's a <i>large</i> amount of overlap, but c'est la vie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T13:25:15-08:00","id":383521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/379105-is-werewolf-going-to-have-a-more-defined-version-of-influence?p=382505#post382505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I haven't read the book, but do you mean that they gain Compelling, Knowing, Unveiling, Ruling, Veiling, and so on equivalents for their Influence, or they get like Spirit \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022?</div> </div> </div> </div>The 14 Practices as related to their Influence, not the actual Arcana trait; and influence 7+ starts granting archmage like abilities. Imperial Mysteries also has stat rules for rank 6+ beings, if you need to use them [I think they're appropriately powerful that even with stats, (non- tier 4) characters can't contest them; but as the old gamer idiom goes &quot;if it has stats, players will kill it&quot;.] I've found it to be a little bit useful in trying to imagine the Shadow cosmology for the Werewolf game I run, but I haven't really ever used its contents. It's very much designed only for archmage chronicles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T13:37:23-08:00","id":383532,"title":"","content":"I suppose I could see that, if it's confined to their Influence. It certainly makes sense for something that powerful to be able to do more than just make, move and strengthen fire, or whatever their Influence is.<br /> <br /> But I agree it also is something only likely to be taken advantage of by archmages or mages. I'm reasonably sure nothing with stats in the Werewolf books has more than 4 dots in any one Influence, even the 2 rank 5 spirits, considered minor gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-27-2015, 04:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}